## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/messaging/scheduled_receipts.dart | ⚠️ important receipt durability — the quiet queue flush and the deliveredids pending counting from the absorbed 2435 impl were dropped without replacement the supersession of 2435 s receipts design probe per append instead of timer backoff drops two pressure window compensations that origin main ships today and neither is replaced 1 no idle flush on main a failed write arms a retry timer 2s → 5min cap precisely because the scheduler may be idle while the descriptor table frees armretry removed in this diff the new drain runs only from write which runs only from append — and receipts are appended only on message lifecycle events scheduled delivered delivery failed scan failed lib src messaging scheduled messages dart a queue that goes quiet after the last delivered receipt fails all messages done table then frees has no further appends so the backlog sits in pending indefinitely and is dropped when the process exits the class doc s core promise — a lost receipt must be impossible a lost receipt a fired timer that cannot be proven fired — no longer holds on exactly the path 2415 is about exit time loss pre existed via dispose dropping pending the idle window did not 2 deliveredids no longer counts pending receipts main counts in memory pending lines as delivered the event happened only its persistence is deferred — collectdelivered loop removed the rewrite reads the disk file only scheduled receipts dart 121 so the obligations ledger reconcile agent cli persist dart reconcileobligationsledger issue 2384 ac1 stops auto closing pending waits whose delivered receipt is deferred — they now ride the age out fallback ac2 instead suggested fix small keep a bounded idle probe — either a low frequency timer or expose void probe hook the scheduler s existing tick so a quiet queue still drains once the table frees — and restore pending line counting in deliveredids also note the pr description still says dispose still drops pending lines — pre existing documented best effort follow up but dispose no longer exists in this design the description and the code disagree about where the loss window is |
