the change actually edits |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | lib/src/env/fd_limit_io.dart | 💡 suggestion fdlimits relaxed the platform gate from macos linux to windows the removed systemfdlimitbackend guarded if platform ismacos platform islinux return null before touching libc the new fdlimits only excludes windows so any other posix flavored host proceeds with rlimitnofile platform ismacos 8 7 — and on a host whose sys resource h numbering differs setrlimit 7 … would modify an unrelated resource on freebsd 7 is rlimit nproc macos 8 linux android 7 and the windows gate are all correct today so nothing supported misbehaves — but restoring the two line ismacos islinux gate costs nothing and re closes the class of wrong resource number bugs on unofficial vm ports suggest dart int soft int hard fdlimits if platform ismacos platform islinux return null |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

